From: Shammah Chancellor <shammah.chancellor@notvalid.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 16:06:11 -0700
Subject: test: flush the logger before reading log-callback counters

Since log lines are written by a logger thread, a callback added with
PushBackCallback (or a DebugLogHelper match function) runs on that thread,
some time after the LogPrintf that produced the line. Two tests read the
counters their callbacks update while the lines could still be queued:

- preconsensus_batch_tests/mempool_batch_untrusted_acceptance_and_
  preconsensus_policy checked parks == 1 and unparks == 1 straight after
  ProcessNewBlock, and failed 3 checks (0 != 1) on 275. Its unparks == 0
  check could also pass without proving anything.
- v2_protocol_handler_tests' 256-transaction burst read checks after
  DeleteCallback, so checks > 0 could fail if no line had been delivered.

Flush before each read, as this commit already does for the wallet and
getarg tests. DebugLogHelper's destructor already flushes, so helpers
checked only after their scope ends are unaffected (mempool_tests, the
AVARESPONSE burst test, ASSERT_DEBUG_LOG users).

Tier: eCash (fixup to ecash/125 logging: write log lines on a logger thread)
